      "writtenOn": "2026-06-22T19:38:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two FDs in play here:\n\nDawn is responsible for closing the original FD (the one you highlighted). When we call ExportInfo, Dawn allows us to borrow the handle integer via .Get(), and closes it when wgpu::SharedFence is destroyed.\n\nFor the new FD, Java is responsible for closing it. Because Dawn will eventually close the original fd, we must call dup(fd) to generate a new handle (dupedFd) pointing to the same sync object.",
      "parentUuid": "08f197a6_f323560d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 486,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 486,
        "endChar": 44
